From d8944763d2be1746df04e6cb9bd928b527b3d960 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Steiner <tomac@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 10:12:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] [iOS] Pick Gemma's backend by GPU family and memory, and
 record its speed

Runs Gemma on the GPU only on Apple GPU family 7 (A14) and later, and
only when loading it there leaves the app at least 1.5 GB from its
memory limit. Everything else runs on the CPU.

On an A13 (family 6, iPhone 11 Pro Max), LiteRT-LM's Metal backend runs
at about 20 tokens per second and produces random tokens, with 16-bit
and 32-bit activations alike. The CPU answers correctly there at 14
tokens per second, first token after 2.5 s, at 0.6 GB of footprint. The
GPU is correct on M-series Macs, and the model card measures it on an
A19 Pro.

Developer launch arguments pick the backend, the CPU thread count, and
the activation precision (-BuiltInAIGemmaBackend,
-BuiltInAIGemmaThreads, -BuiltInAIGemmaActivation), and keep the device
awake while Chrome is in front (-BuiltInAIKeepAwake). After every
answer, Gemma's speed, the start of the answer, and the app's memory
footprint go to Library/Caches/BuiltInAI/stats.jsonl.
